# Before running: pick the `local` environment in the "Run with" selector at the top of the editor,
# and run `npm run http:tokens` once. Without an environment, variables like api and token stay unresolved.
#
# Authentication (RS256 JWT), scopes and tenant isolation (ADR-007, ADR-017).

### 1. No token → 401 UNAUTHENTICATED (+ WWW-Authenticate: Bearer)
GET {{api}}/programs/{{programUsd}}/availability

> {%
    client.test("401", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 401, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.code === "UNAUTHENTICATED", response.body.code);
        client.assert(response.headers.valueOf("WWW-Authenticate") !== null, "WWW-Authenticate header");
    });
%}

### 2. Expired token → 401
GET {{api}}/programs/{{programUsd}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenExpired}}

> {%
    client.test("401", () => client.assert(response.status === 401, "status " + response.status));
%}

### 3. Garbage token → 401
GET {{api}}/programs/{{programUsd}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer not.a.jwt

> {%
    client.test("401", () => client.assert(response.status === 401, "status " + response.status));
%}

### 4. Read-only token can read…
GET {{api}}/programs/{{programUsd}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenReadOnly}}

> {%
    client.test("200", () => client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status));
%}

### 5. …but cannot reserve → 403 INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE
POST {{api}}/programs/{{programUsd}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenReadOnly}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invoiceId": "INV-RO-{{$timestamp}}",
  "amount": { "amountMinor": "1000", "currency": "USD" }
}

> {%
    client.test("403 INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 403, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.code === "INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE", response.body.code);
    });
%}

### 6. Tenant t-2 has its OWN PRG-USD-001 ($2,500,000.00) — same id, different program
GET {{api}}/programs/{{programUsd}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenTenant2}}

> {%
    client.test("t-2 sees its own limit", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.limit.amountMinor === "250000000", response.body.limit.amountMinor);
    });
%}

### 7. t-1's EUR program does not exist for t-2 → 404, not 403 (doesn't reveal it exists)
GET {{api}}/programs/{{programEur}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenTenant2}}

> {%
    client.test("404 PROGRAM_NOT_FOUND", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 404, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.code === "PROGRAM_NOT_FOUND", response.body.code);
    });
%}

### 8. Correlation id: send your own, get it echoed back (and in logs, the ledger and Kafka headers)
GET {{api}}/programs/{{programUsd}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Correlation-Id: phpstorm-demo-{{$timestamp}}

> {%
    client.test("echoed", () => {
        const id = response.headers.valueOf("X-Correlation-Id");
        client.assert(id !== null && id.startsWith("phpstorm-demo-"), "got " + id);
    });
%}
